    <bpmn:process id="W_W4673" name="W4673. Corporate Security Strategy, Charter &amp; Risk-Appetite Framework" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Enterprise risk strategy (VS-33/VS-21.2); board direction; annual review
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: 1 corporate-security strategy &amp; charter
Owner: Chief Security Officer (CSO) / Head of Corporate Security
Participants: CEO, CFO, Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk (VS-21.2), VP Legal (VS-100.3), Board Risk Committee (VS-36), Insurance (VS-26)
Source: workflow W4673 — Corporate Security Strategy, Charter &amp; Risk-Appetite Framework</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4673_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4673_Lane1" name="CSO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4673_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4673_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4673_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4673_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4673_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4673_Start3" name="Enterprise risk strategy (VS-33/VS-21.2); board direction; annual review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4673_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4673_Task4" name="Set the corporate-security strategy and charter: mission, scope (people…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Set the corporate-security strategy and charter: mission, scope (people, principals, assets, reputation), governance (CSO reporting line — typically to CEO/Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk/VP Legal &amp; Compliance), and the risk-appetite for intentional-human-threat exposure (executive protection, travel, investigations)
Responsible (R): CSO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk / VP Legal
Accountable (A): CEO / Board Risk Committee
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4673_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4673_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4673_Task5" name="Align the strategy to enterprise risk management (VS-21.2 W122) and BCP…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Align the strategy to enterprise risk management (VS-21.2 W122) and BCP (VS-26); define the corporate-security risk taxonomy (protective, travel, investigative, workplace-violence, civil-unrest, kidnap/extortion, convergence with cyber VS-27.3) and KRIs
Responsible (R): CSO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4673_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4673_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4673_Task6" name="Obtain board/risk-committee endorsement (VS-36); fund the program (CSO…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Obtain board/risk-committee endorsement (VS-36); fund the program (CSO headcount, GSOC, vendors, insurance — links VS-26 K&amp;R cover); publish the policy enterprise-wide
Responsible (R): CSO / CFO / Board
Accountable (A): CEO / Board
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4673_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4673_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4673_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4673_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-166 (ensure executive-protection &amp; travel-risk control.) | - CTL-707: charter board-endorsed (VS-36); explicit RACI vs. LP/HSE/cyber; risk-appetite documented (VS-21.2)
Owner: Chief Security Officer (CSO) / Head of Corporate Security</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4673_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4673_Annotation8" targetRef="W4673_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4673_Flow10" sourceRef="W4673_Start3" targetRef="W4673_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4673_Flow11" sourceRef="W4673_Task4" targetRef="W4673_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4673_Flow12" sourceRef="W4673_Task5" targetRef="W4673_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4673_Flow13" sourceRef="W4673_Task6" targetRef="W4673_End7" />
    </bpmn:process>
