    <bpmn:process id="W_W4675" name="W4675. Open-Source &amp; Human Intelligence (OSINT/HUMINT) Monitoring &amp; Alerting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous monitoring; alert threshold
Frequency: Continuous (24/7)
Volume: ~25–40 monitored entities (10–20 principal names per W4678, brand/trademark terms, key executives, regions, sourcing destinations)
Owner: Protective Intelligence Lead
Participants: CSO, Legal (VS-100.3), Privacy (VS-91), external intelligence provider
Source: workflow W4675 — Open-Source &amp; Human Intelligence (OSINT/HUMINT) Monitoring &amp; Alerting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4675_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4675_Lane1" name="Protective Intelligence Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4675_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4675_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4675_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4675_Lane2" name="CSO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4675_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4675_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4675_Start4" name="Continuous monitoring; alert threshold">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4675_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4675_Task5" name="Operate OSINT monitoring (news, social media, dark-web mentions of principals…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Operate OSINT monitoring (news, social media, dark-web mentions of principals, brand, threats, protests near sites/HQ, geopolitical events in sourcing destinations VS-122); HUMINT via vetted sources and the guard force (W4677)
Responsible (R): Protective Intelligence Lead / Provider
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4675_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4675_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4675_Task6" name="Triage alerts: filter noise, escalate credible indicators to protective…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Triage alerts: filter noise, escalate credible indicators to protective intelligence (W4674); correlate with internal indicators (HR, LP, cyber VS-27.3 W397) for converged threats
Responsible (R): Protective Intelligence Lead
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Per alert</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4675_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4675_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4675_Task7" name="Govern monitoring within privacy/legal limits (VS-91/VS-100.3 — monitoring…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govern monitoring within privacy/legal limits (VS-91/VS-100.3 — monitoring public OSINT, not unlawful surveillance); retain intelligence per policy (VS-88)
Responsible (R): CSO / Legal / Privacy
Accountable (A): CSO / VP Legal
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4675_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4675_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4675_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4675_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-166 (ensure executive-protection &amp; travel-risk control.) | - CTL-707: monitoring lawful and privacy-compliant (VS-91/VS-100.3); alerts triaged and escalated; intelligence retained per policy
Owner: Protective Intelligence Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
