    <bpmn:process id="W_W4676" name="W4676. Corporate Security Operations Center (GSOC) — 24/7 Monitoring &amp; Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: 24/7 operations; incident alert
Frequency: Continuous (24/7)
Volume: 1 GSOC; ~ monitoring of sites, travel, intelligence, alarms across 200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ + travelers
Owner: GSOC Manager / CSO
Participants: LP (VS-23), Facilities (VS-138), IT/cyber (VS-27.3), BCP (VS-26), guard force (W4677)
Source: workflow W4676 — Corporate Security Operations Center (GSOC) — 24/7 Monitoring &amp; Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4676_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4676_Lane1" name="GSOC Analysts">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4676_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4676_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4676_Lane2" name="GSOC Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4676_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4676_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4676_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4676_Start4" name="24/7 operations; incident alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4676_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4676_Task5" name="Operate the GSOC 24/7: monitor site alarms/CCTV (VS-23/VS-71), traveler…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Operate the GSOC 24/7: monitor site alarms/CCTV (VS-23/VS-71), traveler location (W4687/W4688), intelligence feeds (W4675), and incident channels; triage and dispatch response (guard, LP, law enforcement, medical)
Responsible (R): GSOC Analysts / GSOC Manager
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4676_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4676_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4676_Task6" name="Coordinate response across functions: corporate-security incidents, site…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Coordinate response across functions: corporate-security incidents, site incidents (VS-23/VS-147), cyber incidents (VS-27.3 W383), BCP events (VS-26); maintain the incident command role until handoff (for BCP-class events the handoff lands on the W848 Crisis Management Team per the Event Custody &amp; Precedence Register §3)
Responsible (R): GSOC Manager / CSO
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4676_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4676_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4676_Task7" name="Log every incident, response, and outcome in the case system; produce…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Log every incident, response, and outcome in the case system; produce daily/weekly intelligence &amp; incident summaries for CSO/leadership; feed trend analysis (W4696)
Responsible (R): GSOC Manager
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4676_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4676_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4676_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4676_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-166 (ensure executive-protection &amp; travel-risk control.) | - CTL-707: 24/7 staffing; integrated monitoring; incident-command RACI; every incident logged
Owner: GSOC Manager / CSO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
