    <bpmn:process id="W_W4680" name="W4680. Corporate Security Vendor, Guard-Agency &amp; Investigator Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Vendor selection/renewal; performance issue; TPRM review (VS-161)
Frequency: Per vendor + ongoing oversight
Volume: ~8–15 security vendors (guard agencies, EP providers, intelligence providers, investigation firms, K&amp;R consultant)
Owner: CSO / Corporate Security Vendor Manager
Participants: Procurement (VS-34), TPRM (VS-161), Legal (VS-100.3), Finance (VS-17)
Source: workflow W4680 — Corporate Security Vendor, Guard-Agency &amp; Investigator Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4680_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4680_Lane1" name="CSO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4680_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4680_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4680_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4680_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4680_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4680_Start3" name="Vendor selection/renewal; performance issue; TPRM review (VS-161)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4680_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4680_Task4" name="Select and contract corporate-security vendors (guard agencies, EP providers…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Select and contract corporate-security vendors (guard agencies, EP providers, intelligence/investigation firms) via procurement (VS-34) and TPRM due diligence (VS-161): licensure (PNP-SOSIA for security agencies), vetting, insurance, confidentiality
Responsible (R): CSO / Procurement / TPRM
Accountable (A): CSO / CFO
Duration: Per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4680_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4680_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4680_Task5" name="Govern vendor performance against SLA (guard quality, EP responsiveness…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Govern vendor performance against SLA (guard quality, EP responsiveness, intelligence timeliness); manage the lifecycle (renewal/exit per VS-67/VS-161); enforce confidentiality and data-handling (VS-91)
Responsible (R): CSO / Vendor Manager
Accountable (A): CSO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4680_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4680_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4680_Task6" name="Assure vendor conduct (no rights-abuses, no corruption — links VS-86/VS-119)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Assure vendor conduct (no rights-abuses, no corruption — links VS-86/VS-119); manage conflicts of interest and sole-source justification for sensitive services
Responsible (R): CSO / Legal / Ethics
Accountable (A): CSO / VP Legal
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4680_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4680_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4680_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4680_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-707 (ensure controlled execution — Corporate Security Strategy, Threat Intelligence &amp; Risk Framework (PA-159.1).) | - CTL-707: vendors licensed/vetted (VS-161); SLA-managed; confidentiality and conduct assured (VS-86/VS-91/VS-119)
Owner: CSO / Corporate Security Vendor Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
